## How the Prototype Addresses the Business Problem

> **The Core Operational Challenge:** In routine gas chromatography (`GC2`) quality control, analysts either spend excessive time manually reviewing normal, passing runs or miss subtle, early-stage instrument drift—while introducing generative AI directly into lab operations risks false alarms, hallucinated root causes, and compliance violations.

By intentionally scoping the prototype to **one instrument (`GC2`)**, **one SPC workflow**, and **one conditional AI-review path**, our focused two-step architecture solves this problem across three key areas:

| Operational Pain Point | Prototype Solution | Business & Quality Impact |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Alert Fatigue & Missed Drift** | **Rule-Based Power BI Screening:** Deterministic math rules screen every run against fixed lab-standard limits before any AI is invoked. | Routine runs pass silently with zero alerts, while genuine **Out-of-Control (OOC)** spikes and subtle **six-point trends** are caught early. Malformed records are isolated via a `DQ_Flag` so broken data feeds never trigger false investigations. |
| **Slow Manual Lookups** | **Power Automate Context Bundling:** A user-triggered flow packages the flagged run, the prior 10 valid runs, and 3 days of environmental telemetry (`DailyLogs.xlsx`) into one structured payload. | Eliminates manual cross-referencing across spreadsheets and chromatograms during an investigation while enforcing strict data isolation. |
| **AI Hallucinations & Compliance Risk** | **Guardrailed Advisory Output:** Prompts restrict the AI to strictly *advisory* explanations grounded solely in the supplied JSON payload. | Explicitly flags missing environmental logs (e.g., `TC05`) rather than inventing context, and routes concrete checks to `AI_Review_Log.xlsx`—keeping physical verification, batch holds, and final dispositions firmly under human and lab-manager authority. |
